<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75572" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄσσε</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τώ,</span>
		prop. neut. dual, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the two
			eyes,</i> nom. and acc. freq. in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, who however adds the Adj. in the pl., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄ. φαεινά, αἱματόεντα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				13.435
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				616
			</span></i> (dual 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαεινώ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					14.236
				</span></i>
			): and the Verb in the sg., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρὶ δ᾽ ὄ. δεδήει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					12.466
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀξύτατον κεφαλῆς ἒκ δέρκεται ὄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					23.477
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν δέ οἱ ὄ. δαίεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					6.131
				</span></i>
			 : later gen. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄσσων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					826
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				400
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.Epigr.</u>
				3.400.5
			</span></i> (Delph., <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>); dat. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄσσοις, ὄσσοισι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				145
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				426
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				430
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sapph.
				29
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				144
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				679
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ag.</u>
				469
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1231
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ichn.</u>
				47
			</span></i>, etc.; <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				58.28
			</span></i> cites also dat. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄσσει,</span> and <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> gen. pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀσσέων.</span> (Prob. I.-<i><span class="en">
				E.
			</span></i>
			<i>oq[uglide]-ye,</i> cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄσσομαι,
				ὄψομαι.</span>)</div>
